<ArticleLayout
  title="Blue Economy, Agriculture & Livelihoods"
  description="Coastal fisher safety, mangrove restoration with beekeeping, circular agro-ecosystems and women-led food processing in Sierra Leone."
>
  <p>
    Coastal and agricultural livelihoods depend directly on the health
    of the land and water around them. This area supports both the
    income and the ecosystem at the same time.
  </p>

  <h2>What this covers</h2>
  <p>
    A coastal fisher safety and cold-chain cooperative model improves
    safety equipment and post-catch handling, so less of what is caught
    is lost before it reaches a buyer. A blue-green resilience project
    restores mangroves while adding a beekeeping livelihood component,
    giving the community a direct income reason to protect the
    ecosystem it depends on.
  </p>
  <p>
    A circular agro-ecosystem programme, running as a first-year bridge
    pilot with a larger multi-year phase in development with European
    research partners, connects agricultural production, waste and soil
    health into one system. A women-led mango value-addition project
    turns surplus mango into processed, packaged products with a real
    sales channel.
  </p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>
    Each project is designed so environmental protection and household
    income sit inside the same activity, reinforcing each other over
    time.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
